// Title: Bad Opsec Defaults Sacrificial Processes With Improper Arguments
// ID: a7c3d773-caef-227e-a7e7-c2f13c622329
// Status: test
// Level: high
// Author: Oleg Kolesnikov @securonix invrep_de, oscd.community, Florian Roth (Nextron Systems), Christian Burkard (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2020-10-23
// Tags: attack.stealth, attack.t1218.011
// Description: Detects attackers using tooling with bad opsec defaults.
// E.g. spawning a sacrificial process to inject a capability into the process without taking into account how the process is normally run.
// One trivial example of this is using rundll32.exe without arguments as a sacrificial process (default in CS, now highlighted by c2lint), running WerFault without arguments (Kraken - credit am0nsec), and other examples.
// Converted by: Sigma Universal SIEM/EDR CLI

process where (((process.executable endswith "\\regasm.exe" and process.command_line endswith "regasm.exe") or (process.executable endswith "\\regsvcs.exe" and process.command_line endswith "regsvcs.exe") or (process.executable endswith "\\regsvr32.exe" and process.command_line endswith "regsvr32.exe") or (process.executable endswith "\\rundll32.exe" and process.command_line endswith "rundll32.exe") or (process.executable endswith "\\WerFault.exe" and process.command_line endswith "WerFault.exe")) and not ((((process.parent.executable like "*_\\AppData\\Local\\BraveSoftware\\Brave-Browser\\Application\\*" or process.parent.executable like "*_\\AppData\\Local\\Google\\Chrome\\Application\\*") and process.parent.executable endswith "\\Installer\\setup.exe" and process.parent.command_line like "*_--uninstall *" and process.executable endswith "\\rundll32.exe" and process.command_line endswith "rundll32.exe") or (process.parent.executable like "*_\\AppData\\Local\\Microsoft\\EdgeUpdate\\Install\\{*" and process.executable endswith "\\rundll32.exe" and process.command_line endswith "rundll32.exe"))))
